{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"8ad75ea14f1a3fd0bb29bb5b1596b76cc9a0d48e5e9dc6ad2ba5aedd8316bd1b","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_dca78456c3c4d40c75b9bd5a2dc9fa9299713b6b95487f28bd2eafb9b04b9e6a","overall_assessment":"The paper presents a technically sound and well-motivated study of adversarial training at scale, with clear methodological contributions and a strong empirical foundation. The authors are careful in their reporting, explicitly acknowledging limitations such as the lack of robustness to iterative attacks and the label-leaking artifact. The experimental design is comprehensive, utilizing a large-scale dataset and diverse model architectures, though the absence of statistical significance testing and code availability slightly limits the reproducibility and statistical rigor of the findings.","paper_id":"BJm4T4Kgx","paper_identity_sha256":"a630c50de5af543b5ae81054178e254bb9d55a8a1b0538a03067d55e41292004","prompt_identity_sha256":"a444c51b50c27cc1483142271f02d8a4d74f154f27a88b2e4a5dddd178019dc2","raw_response_sha256":"478d44332f07886b1bb9caa7926c004cb7e8dc3bbbd747d2be79bef69396a87f","request_identity_sha256":"acd305d8f9f476317b1de590d606a2dab7e8c1f5155b60f7f4e95b3e6e1d1cfa","reviewer_identity_sha256":"32b29c26fbf1508e066dfb25b1a9a3fe0654c5869a7da3020e1e8e61940befe3","role":"QUAL","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v4","structural_context_sha256":"f0c1b6e5f5554b16f648d1796c97a3329a9fe0059b455d247cf73f07d0e07551","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-012","SRC-013","SRC-014"],"review_text":"The proposed adversarial training algorithm is well-formulated and mathematically consistent. The authors provide a clear loss function that allows for independent control of the number and relative weight of adversarial examples, and they specify the use of a truncated normal distribution for the perturbation magnitude to ensure robustness across different epsilon values. The algorithm is correctly implemented as described in Algorithm 1, and the authors provide a logical explanation for the observed 'label leaking' effect, identifying it as a consequence of the model exploiting regularities in the adversarial example construction process. No major conceptual or implementation errors are apparent in the methodological description.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-MET"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-014","SRC-016","SRC-019","SRC-021","SRC-024","SRC-028","SRC-031"],"review_text":"The experimental design is comprehensive and appropriate for the claims made. The authors use the ImageNet dataset, which is a standard and large-scale benchmark, and they evaluate their method on both Inception v3 and v4 models. They include a variety of baselines, including standard training and different adversarial training methods, and they use both top-1 and top-5 accuracy as evaluation metrics. The ablation studies are thorough, examining the effects of model capacity, the delay of adversarial training, and the use of different regularization techniques. The experiments convincingly validate the claims that adversarial training increases robustness to one-step attacks and that model capacity can improve robustness.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-EXP"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-014","SRC-015","SRC-016"],"review_text":"The paper provides sufficient detail to reproduce the technical process, including the use of the RMSProp optimizer, a learning rate of 0.045, and a minibatch size of 32. The authors also specify the use of 50 machines for synchronous distributed training and the number of training iterations (150k). However, the paper does not provide a link to the code or a detailed description of the dataset splits, which could hinder full reproducibility. The hyperparameters for the adversarial training process, such as the value of lambda and the number of adversarial examples in the minibatch, are clearly stated, which is a strength.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-REP"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-004","SRC-005","SRC-017","SRC-031"],"review_text":"The paper sufficiently compares against relevant prior work and state-of-the-art methods. The authors cite and compare their results with previous work on adversarial training, such as Goodfellow et al. (2014) and Miyato et al. (2016b;a), and they provide a clear explanation for the differences in their results. They also compare their method against different types of adversarial example generation methods, including FGSM, one-step target class methods, and iterative methods. The literature review is thorough and up-to-date, and the authors properly position their work within the context of existing research.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-CMP"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-016","SRC-019","SRC-021","SRC-024"],"review_text":"The paper does not report statistical significance tests or confidence intervals for the reported improvements. The authors mention that the changes in accuracy for a small delay of adversarial training were 'not statistically significant,' but they do not provide the specific statistical tests or p-values used to make this determination. The results are based on single runs of the experiments, and the variance across different random seeds is not reported. This lack of statistical rigor limits the ability to determine whether the observed improvements are statistically meaningful or due to chance.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-STA"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"5fe0372fbef372e156e039df87e4b158e129e4ab97baab34a6db205f8071e6bb","paper_id":"BJm4T4Kgx","paper_ordinal":37,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"478d44332f07886b1bb9caa7926c004cb7e8dc3bbbd747d2be79bef69396a87f","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"BJm4T4Kgx","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"1b2e919acc3de45f8c00346e8f200031d9fd332cee8539a104a3532b527ede13","request_identity_sha256":"acd305d8f9f476317b1de590d606a2dab7e8c1f5155b60f7f4e95b3e6e1d1cfa","role":"QUAL","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v6","usage":{"completion_tokens":1127,"prompt_tokens":19171,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":20298},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"acd305d8f9f476317b1de590d606a2dab7e8c1f5155b60f7f4e95b3e6e1d1cfa","role":"QUAL","role_ordinal":0,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v4"}